; -COO- group: formed by condensation of carboxylic acid + alcohol.
; R-COOH + HO-R' → R-COO-R' + H2O  (esterification, acid-catalysed)
; the reverse reaction is hydrolysis (saponification with base → soap).
; 
; esters have pleasant fruity or floral smells — used in flavours and perfumes.
; ethyl acetate: nail polish remover, glue solvent.
; isoamyl acetate: banana flavour.
; methyl salicylate: wintergreen.
; 
; fats and oils are triglycerides — triesters of glycerol + three fatty acids.
; saturated fats: solid at room temperature (lard, butter). all single bonds.
; unsaturated fats: liquid (oils). one or more C=C double bonds.
; trans fats: unsaturated but trans geometry — behave like saturated.
; 
; polymers: polyesters — PET (polyethylene terephthalate) — bottles, fabric.
; formed by condensation polymerisation of diacid + diol.
; waxes: long-chain esters. beeswax, carnauba wax, ear wax.

